  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & 15 \\\\ 15 & 26\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
